{"title":"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a719b049c276e55a58cfb22c3e914b3cce1a7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\cos 0^\\circ \\cos 1^\\circ} +  \\frac{1}{\\cos 1^\\circ \\cos 2^\\circ} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{\\cos 88^\\circ \\cos 89^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 1^\\circ}{\\sin^2 1^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"471\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d6789639e5749f4fa51e6d985a16d892bab09fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_k = (1, \\tan k^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> in the coordinate plane with origin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e1baf8d541d0a7887587d42b5175432b680eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a0832f43dd98f16bbf145242129df3eb4daf743e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k \\le 89$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a567c74f164bab3839fc015b072847313afa6e5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(1); pair O=(0,0), a=expi(0), b=expi(1/6), c=expi(2/6), d=expi(3/6), y=expi(32/30), z= expi(34/30); pair A=a, B=b/b.x, C= c/c.x, D=d/d.x, Y=y/y.x, Z=z/z.x, E=(D+Y)/2; pair X=(O+E)/2; draw(O--A--Z); draw(B--O--C--D--O--Y--Z--O); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,O,SW); label(&quot;\\(M_0\\)&quot;,A,ESE); label(&quot;\\(M_1\\)&quot;,B,ESE); label(&quot;\\(M_2\\)&quot;,C,ESE); label(&quot;\\(M_3\\)&quot;,D,ESE); label(&quot;\\(\\vdots\\)&quot;,E,ESE); label(&quot;\\(M_{88}\\)&quot;,Y,ESE); label(&quot;\\(M_{89}\\)&quot;,Z,ESE); label(&quot;\\(\\ddots\\)&quot;,X); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"335\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Evidently, the angle between segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8bd2ef6c39842098734a4e2cd4f26d6e6d4bee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/a/77a44321ed1461794258fcb2e2abccfd733e02aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d36e7f46641a6512c7847067b8441d770a9848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b-a)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, and the length of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8bd2ef6c39842098734a4e2cd4f26d6e6d4bee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/5522a89a58154efdf070de45e96138a7a7416b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/\\cos a^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.  It then follows that the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/95005ecf75040fc42be57d29487091bfe0cb9a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_aOM_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db86a4f1a9e4c999236139ec9e0eb0dd20aa7606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{2} \\sin(b-a)^\\circ \\cdot OM_a \\cdot OM_b = \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sin(b-a)^\\circ / (\\cos a^\\circ \\cdot \\cos b^\\circ)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"446\" height=\"21\" />.  Therefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef9a1188bfdd3d1fd88bd74cf61298babcc18194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=0}^{88} \\frac{\\tfrac{1}{2} \\sin 1^\\circ}{ \\cos k^\\circ \\cos k+1^\\circ} &amp;= \\sum_{k=0}^{88} [ M_k O M_{k+1} ] \\\\ &amp;= [ M_0 O M_{89} ] \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{ \\tfrac{1}{2} \\sin 89^\\circ}{\\cos 89^\\circ} = \\frac{\\tfrac{1}{2} \\cos 1^\\circ}{\\sin 1^\\circ} , \\end{align*}\" width=\"339\" height=\"126\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32b10fa7d198ad236d79c8c2acef1eb9d3b10ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{88} \\frac{1}{\\cos k^\\circ \\cos (k+1)^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 1^\\circ}{ \\sin^2 1^\\circ},\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"50\" />\nas desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First multiply both sides of the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d58526eeb860c80db28bf288527346e455b2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, so the right hand side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a038e89987e91b89bf5b8a12d3b6179ea4310a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cos 1}{\\sin 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />.  Now by rewriting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeb707a893da76f181261ab71174cc0cc1d325a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 1=\\sin((k+1)-k)=\\sin(k+1)\\cos(k)+\\sin(k)\\cos(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"486\" height=\"18\" />, we can derive the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff627ecfb7e8b22a055ddb5084a22c6aa30af1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(n+1)-\\tan(n)=\\frac{\\sin 1}{\\cos(n)\\cos(n+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"316\" height=\"41\" />.  Then the left hand side of the equation simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425a815150758355506a5a4483a305e4b1d29fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 89-\\tan 0=\\tan 89=\\frac{\\sin 89}{\\cos 89}=\\frac{\\cos 1}{\\sin 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"316\" height=\"38\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b4444d0349f1941e146e187df441670947f617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. We get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1bb437ffde8d7ebee55d5fab412afdf0105997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sin{1}}{\\cos{0}\\cos{1}} + \\frac {\\sin{1}}{\\cos{1}\\cos{2}} + ... + \\frac {\\sin{1}}{\\cos{88}\\cos{89}} = \\frac {\\cos{1}}{\\sin{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"402\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>we can write this as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e73b94515daa166b4154c8941633b0e4726426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sin{1 - 0}}{\\cos{0}\\cos{1}} + \\frac {\\sin{2 - 1}}{\\cos{1}\\cos{2}} + ... + \\frac {\\sin{89 - 88}}{\\cos{88}\\cos{89}} = \\frac {\\cos{1}}{\\sin{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"402\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This is an identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e28e03212d90f97f4941f2c1c167fa670094db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{a} - \\tan{b} = \\frac {\\sin{(a - b)}}{\\cos{a}\\cos{b}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"204\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore;\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2560498b14e19fefe27441fd393ba7d5418391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i = 1}^{89}[\\tan{k} - \\tan{(k - 1)}] = \\tan{89} - \\tan{0} = \\cot{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"374\" height=\"50\" />, because of telescoping. \n</p><p>but since we multiplied <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b4444d0349f1941e146e187df441670947f617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> in the beginning, we need to divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b4444d0349f1941e146e187df441670947f617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. So we get that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec88a5ef94395b98973469041d509b1f648b7f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{\\cos{0}\\cos{1}} + \\frac {1}{\\cos{1}\\cos{2}} + \\frac {1}{\\cos{2}\\cos{3}} + .... + \\frac {1}{\\cos{88}\\cos{89}} = \\frac {\\cos{1}}{\\sin^2{1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"515\" height=\"38\" />\nas desired. QED\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b44c5804bae4d1723e93b36f3f89c085678bc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac{1}{\\cos 0^\\circ\\cos 1^\\circ} + \\frac{1}{\\cos 1^\\circ\\cos 2^\\circ} + ... + \\frac{1}{\\cos 88^\\circ\\cos 89^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"420\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352404bde5b339d5da72a79b265065580be77d94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 1^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f36b18b782733f99b8710548129bf783527291b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S \\sin 1^\\circ = \\frac{\\sin(1^\\circ-0^\\circ)}{\\cos 0^\\circ\\cos 1^\\circ} + ... + \\frac{\\sin(89^\\circ-88^\\circ)}{\\cos 88^\\circ\\cos 89^\\circ}\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/1499a09813a2831e923c5de6196907c5d0fd8049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin((x+1^\\circ)-x)}{\\cos 0^\\circ\\cos 1^\\circ} = \\tan (x+1^\\circ) - \\tan x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"312\" height=\"39\" /> after expanding the sine, and so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85c00ea9496e29cf73e3206e9ce1c39d7d1cc57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S \\sin 1^\\circ = \\left(\\tan 1^\\circ - \\tan 0^\\circ\\right) + \\cdots + \\left(\\tan 89^\\circ - \\tan 88^\\circ\\right) = \\tan 89^\\circ - \\tan 0^\\circ = \\cot 1^\\circ = \\frac{\\cos 1^\\circ}{\\sin 1^\\circ},\\]\" width=\"689\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41ce6be141abcf2b9c00463ff9e0d6229f969d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\frac{\\cos 1^\\circ}{\\sin^21^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO\" title=\"1992 USAMO\">1992 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=356413#p356413\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183504\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 224/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8349/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.601      1 -total\n 55.19%    6.954      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.32%    5.333      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6315:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183504 and revision id 79519. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}